{"_id": "tour-olumo-rock-abeokuta", "_type": "tour", "name": "Olumo Rock, Abeokuta", "slug": {"_type": "slug", "current": "olumo-rock-abeokuta"}, "destination": "Abeokuta, Ogun State", "category": "Cultural Journeys", "shortDescription": "Visit Olumo Rock in Abeokuta, the natural fortress that sheltered the Egba people, with caves, shrines and views over the city.", "fullDescription": [{"_type": "block", "_key": "b1", "style": "normal", "markDefs": [], "children": [{"_type": "span", "_key": "c1", "text": "Olumo Rock rises about 137 metres above sea level in Abeokuta, Ogun State. In the 19th century it served the Egba people as a natural fortress, offering shelter and a lookout during inter-tribal wars. The name Abeokuta is commonly translated from Yoruba as \u201cunder the rock\u201d.", "marks": []}]}, {"_type": "block", "_key": "b2", "style": "normal", "markDefs": [], "children": [{"_type": "span", "_key": "c2", "text": "The site is also culturally important: its patron spirit is venerated in Yoruba religion, and caves, rock shelters and shrine areas around the rock show how it has been used over time. From the top there are wide views across Abeokuta.", "marks": []}]}, {"_type": "block", "_key": "b3", "style": "normal", "markDefs": [], "children": [{"_type": "span", "_key": "c3", "text": "Please confirm itinerary details, price and dates with Plum Tree Tours when you enquire.", "marks": []}]}], "highlights": ["A natural fortress used by the Egba people in the 19th century", "Caves, rock shelters and shrine areas", "Views over Abeokuta from the rock"], "duration": 1, "currency": "NGN", "tourImage": {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/cover.jpg"}, "gallery": [{"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/abeokuta-100.jpg", "_key": "g0"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/abeokuta-103.jpg", "_key": "g1"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/abeokuta-104.jpg", "_key": "g2"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/abeokuta-107.jpg", "_key": "g3"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/abeokuta-109.jpg", "_key": "g4"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/abeokuta-113.jpg", "_key": "g5"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/abeokuta-city-30.jpg", "_key": "g6"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/an-entrance-of-the-cave-in-olumo-rock.jpg", "_key": "g7"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/hide-out-cave-during-19th-century-egba-war.jpg", "_key": "g8"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/olumo-3.jpg", "_key": "g9"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/olumo-4.jpg", "_key": "g10"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/olumo-shrine.jpg", "_key": "g11"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/olumo-rock/picture-author-14.jpg", "_key": "g12"}], "featured": true, "isPublished": true}
{"_id": "tour-zuma-rock", "_type": "tour", "name": "Zuma Rock, Abuja", "slug": {"_type": "slug", "current": "zuma-rock-abuja"}, "destination": "Zuma Rock, Niger State (near Abuja)", "category": "Wildlife and Safari", "shortDescription": "See Zuma Rock, the huge monolith beside the Abuja\u2013Kaduna road, known as the Gateway to Abuja.", "fullDescription": [{"_type": "block", "_key": "b1", "style": "normal", "markDefs": [], "children": [{"_type": "span", "_key": "c1", "text": "Zuma Rock is a massive monolith near Madalla in Suleja, Niger State, beside the Abuja\u2013Kaduna road. It rises roughly 725 metres above sea level and is sometimes called the \u201cGateway to Abuja\u201d.", "marks": []}]}, {"_type": "block", "_key": "b2", "style": "normal", "markDefs": [], "children": [{"_type": "span", "_key": "c2", "text": "The rock is formed from an igneous intrusion of gabbro and granodiorite, and it has long been significant to local communities. It also appears on the Nigerian 100-naira banknote.", "marks": []}]}, {"_type": "block", "_key": "b3", "style": "normal", "markDefs": [], "children": [{"_type": "span", "_key": "c3", "text": "Please confirm itinerary details, price and dates with Plum Tree Tours when you enquire.", "marks": []}]}], "highlights": ["A giant monolith rising about 725 m above sea level", "Known as the Gateway to Abuja", "Appears on the 100-naira note"], "duration": 1, "currency": "NGN", "tourImage": {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/zuma-rock/cover.jpg"}, "gallery": [{"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/zuma-rock/a-rock-in-abuja-dei-dei.jpg", "_key": "g0"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/zuma-rock/abujia-zuma-rock-panoramio.jpg", "_key": "g1"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/zuma-rock/behind-the-world-famous-zuma-rock-along-abuja-kaduna-1.jpg", "_key": "g2"}, {"_type": "image", "_sanityAsset": "image@file://./images/tours/zuma-ro